[Music]  hi I'm Scott a snowy and I'm Angie Rito  and we are the chef owners of Don äôt  restaurant in the West Village we're  both really passionate about  italian-american food and we basically  put our own twist on classic Italian  dishes such as lasagna instead of doing  a traditional layer of lasagna we do  basically like pinwheels Angie was  looking at a picture on Instagram of  like cinnamon buns or something a light  bulb went off in her head and she was  like oh it'd be cool if we can make  lasagna like in that form and it ended  up being a really smart idea and also  growing up we would eat lasagna  everybody always wants like the crispy  ends which is usually typically only the  four corners but when you cook it like  this the entire top gets really crispy  it's like the perfect balance everybody  gets like a crispy part and then the  soft part and it's much lighter because  it's not compacted like a traditional  [Music]  the way we make the lasagna here is we  take fresh pasta sheets that we make  in-house we cook them briefly in boiling  salted water cooled them down then we  spread a layer of bechamel ax on top on  top of that we add a layer of Parmesan  cheese a good amount of mozzarella  cheese we had a second layer of pasta on  top of that we put a generous helping of  our bolognese sauce which sort of like a  typical Bolognese but we add a couple of  unique ingredients to it we had Italian  sausage pancetta  we had some Rosano tomatoes after we  spread the layer of Bolognese we add a  small layer of bechamel at the top to  sort of seal the roll closed once we  roll it up and at that point you roll it  seal it closed  cool it down and then we slice it into  pinwheels and we place the pinwheels in  a casserole dish with San Marzano tomato  sauce some dollops of fresh robiola  cheese we decided to use robiola cheese  instead of ricotta cheese which is  typically used in  lasagnas because it has a tankiness to  it and it's also it has a very light  texture so it makes it though the dish  overall come off as a lot lighter we put  it in a 400 degree oven for about 12 to  15 minutes when we take it out of the  oven we finish it with olive oil and  fresh chopped parsley and that's the  process our style of food is a new take  on Italian American food like a modern  Italian American restaurant I feel like  especially in New York City you know the  markets a little bit saturated with  Italian American restaurants so we  wanted to do something unique and  different there are a couple sort of  iconic restaurants in New York you know  Don Antonio Don Peppe and it's always a  man's name so this is sort of like you  know it's supposed to be a little bit  cheeky but it's like I'm the matriarch  good god we're both really passionate  about what we do and we both I don't  think can see ourselves doing anything  else and this allows us to do it  together  [Music]

